<title>AUSTRALIA: CBA seeing strong interest for bond issue.</title>
<headline>CBA seeing strong interest for bond issue.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commonwealth Bank of Australia (CBA) is about to officially launch a fixed interest bond on the Australian domestic debt market, and preliminary interest has been strong, a bank official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The size of the issue has been increased to A$400 million from an initial planned size of around A$250 million.</p>
<p>The bonds will mature on April 15, 2000 and will carry a coupon of 6-3/4 percent. Pricing will be later on Thursday.</p>
<p>--Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
